{"event":"step_update","step_update":{"conversation_id":"09feddb6-4324-467f-a201-46d03ae11167","step_index":40,"state":"DONE","step_type":"tool","tool_name":"run_command","duration_seconds":0.901625,"tool_info":{"name":"run_command","parameters":{"CommandLine":"grep -rn \"INQUIRE IN GRAPHRAG CHAT\" . --exclude-dir=node_modules --exclude-dir=.git"},"output":"./functional_specification_005/scan_report_001.md:230:| **DEF-06** | Canvas Node Click Assistant Drawer Integration (`functional_specification_005.md` Section 3, Section 4.5) | Clicking \"INQUIRE IN GRAPHRAG CHAT\" in `NodeDetailDrawer.tsx` or submitting single node PKs to `/api/graphrag/subgraph` in `routes.py#L286-L352` maps single PKs to slot `\"entity\"` and calls `extract_connecting_subgraph`, which fails with `TraversalError`. | Single-node canvas inspection crashes the assistant drawer instead of retrieving surrounding relationships. |\r\n./functional_specification_005/scan_reports/scan_report_001_plan_scan_1.md:230:| **DEF-06** | Canvas Node Click Assistant Drawer Integration (`functional_specification_005.md` Section 3, Section 4.5) | Clicking \"INQUIRE IN GRAPHRAG CHAT\" in `NodeDetailDrawer.tsx` or submitting single node PKs to `/api/graphrag/subgraph` in `routes.py#L286-L352` maps single PKs to slot `\"entity\"` and calls `extract_connecting_subgraph`, which fails with `TraversalError`. | Single-node canvas inspection crashes the assistant drawer instead of retrieving surrounding relationships. |\r\n./functional_specification_005/by_agent/plan-scan-1/scan_report_001.md:230:| **DEF-06** | Canvas Node Click Assistant Drawer Integration (`functional_specification_005.md` Section 3, Section 4.5) | Clicking \"INQUIRE IN GRAPHRAG CHAT\" in `NodeDetailDrawer.tsx` or submitting single node PKs to `/api/graphrag/subgraph` in `routes.py#L286-L352` maps single PKs to slot `\"entity\"` and calls `extract_connecting_subgraph`, which fails with `TraversalError`. | Single-node canvas inspection crashes the assistant drawer instead of retrieving surrounding relationships. |\r\n./functional_specification_005/by_agent/plan-scan-1/scan_reports/scan_report_001_plan_scan_1.md:230:| **DEF-06** | Canvas Node Click Assistant Drawer Integration (`functional_specification_005.md` Section 3, Section 4.5) | Clicking \"INQUIRE IN GRAPHRAG CHAT\" in `NodeDetailDrawer.tsx` or submitting single node PKs to `/api/graphrag/subgraph` in `routes.py#L286-L352` maps single PKs to slot `\"entity\"` and calls `extract_connecting_subgraph`, which fails with `TraversalError`. | Single-node canvas inspection crashes the assistant drawer instead of retrieving surrounding relationships. |\r\n./functional_specification_007.md:12:This specification defines the functional requirements for refining the **\"INQUIRE IN GRAPHRAG CHAT\"** action button located in the node detail inspection drawer.\r\n./functional_specification_007.md:15:Currently, clicking the \"INQUIRE IN GRAPHRAG CHAT\" button in the node detail drawer only opens the chat drawer. It does not submit an inquiry, does not pass the selected node's identity to the backend, and leaves the user with an empty input box. Furthermore, if a user manually types the node's title (such as *\"Consolidated Appropriations Act, 2023\"*), the query fails with zero nodes illuminated because the node primary key was discarded rather than passed to the retrieval engine.\r\n./functional_specification_007.md:18:Clicking \"INQUIRE IN GRAPHRAG CHAT\" must act as an active, one-click intelligence trigger. It must automatically open the chat interface, submit a contextual inquiry focused on the selected node, pass the node's explicit primary key (`primary_key`) to the GraphRAG pipeline, retrieve the connected graph lineage from Neo4j, and render the grounded LLM synthesis while illuminating the active path on the canvas.\r\n./functional_specification_007.md:28:* **`{functionality}`:** Seamless end-to-end user workflow where selecting any entity on the visualizer canvas and clicking \"INQUIRE IN GRAPHRAG CHAT\" immediately produces a grounded, conversational analysis of that entity and illuminates its path on the canvas.\r\n./functional_specification_007.md:56:   * The \"INQUIRE IN GRAPHRAG CHAT\" button is active whenever any node on the blueprint canvas is selected and displayed in the node detail drawer.\r\n./functional_specification_007.md:108:   * If a user clicks a different node and presses \"INQUIRE IN GRAPHRAG CHAT\", the system must process the new inquiry as a distinct turn in the conversation thread without clearing prior messages.\r\n./functional_specification_007.md:118:1. **One-Click Execution:** Clicking \"INQUIRE IN GRAPHRAG CHAT\" on any node opens the chat drawer and immediately generates an in-thread response without requiring manual typing.\r\n./src/frontend/src/components/NodeDetailDrawer.tsx:264:          ◈ INQUIRE IN GRAPHRAG CHAT\r\n"}}}
